msgid ""
msgstr ""
"# Layer Normalization Example\n"
"\n"
"This document demonstrates how to use the Layer Normalization (LayerNorm) module in the OneFlow deep learning framework. Layer Normalization is a technique used to stabilize and accelerate the training of deep neural networks by normalizing the activations of a layer across the feature dimension.\n"
"\n"
"## Overview\n"
"\n"
"Layer Normalization computes the mean and variance of the inputs across the feature dimension for each training sample independently, and then normalizes the inputs using these statistics. This helps in reducing internal covariate shift and improving the convergence speed of the model.\n"
"\n"
"## Usage\n"
"\n"
"To use the LayerNorm module, you need to import it from the OneFlow library and instantiate it with the desired parameters. The following example shows how to apply LayerNorm to a tensor.\n"
"\n"
"```python\n"
"import oneflow as flow\n"
"import oneflow.nn as nn\n"
"\n"
"# Create a LayerNorm module with normalized shape [feature_dim]\n"
"layer_norm = nn.LayerNorm(normalized_shape=[feature_dim])\n"
"\n"
"# Input tensor of shape [batch_size, feature_dim]\n"
"input_tensor = flow.randn(batch_size, feature_dim)\n"
"\n"
"# Apply LayerNorm\n"
"output_tensor = layer_norm(input_tensor)\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"## Parameters\n"
"\n"
"- `normalized_shape`: The shape of the features to be normalized. This can be an integer or a list of integers.\n"
"- `eps`: A small value added to the denominator for numerical stability (default: 1e-5).\n"
"- `elementwise_affine`: A boolean indicating whether to apply learnable affine transformation (default: True).\n"
"\n"
"## Example\n"
"\n"
"Here is a complete example demonstrating the use of LayerNorm in a simple neural network.\n"
"\n"
"```python\n"
"import oneflow as flow\n"
"import oneflow.nn as nn\n"
"\n"
"class SimpleModel(nn.Module):\n"
"    def __init__(self):\n"
"        super(SimpleModel, self).__init__()\n"
"        self.fc1 = nn.Linear(128, 64)\n"
"        self.ln = nn.LayerNorm(64)\n"
"        self.fc2 = nn.Linear(64, 10)\n"
"\n"
"    def forward(self, x):\n"
"        x = self.fc1(x)\n"
"        x = self.ln(x)\n"
"        x = flow.relu(x)\n"
"        x = self.fc2(x)\n"
"        return x\n"
"\n"
"model = SimpleModel()\n"
"input_data = flow.randn(32, 128)\n"
"output = model(input_data)\n"
"print(output.shape)\n"
"```\n"
"\n"
"In this example, the LayerNorm is applied after the first fully connected layer to normalize the activations before the ReLU activation function.\n"
"\n"
"## Conclusion\n"
"\n"
"Layer Normalization is a powerful tool for improving the training stability and performance of deep learning models. The OneFlow framework provides a simple and efficient implementation of this technique, making it easy to integrate into your models.\n"

